// The test's ambient (docs/spec/rows.md, Entry 5; runtime.md, Tests 10):
// the authority a test has to reach the host, confined to a folder of its
// own. A test never holds the prelude's Ambient. A named context whose
// header says `needs testing.Ambient` may make the confined host providers
// (fs.NewTestHost, exec.NewTestHost, os.NewTestHost) while it is built:
//
//	let onHost = context needs testing.Ambient { exec.Runner: exec.NewTestHost() }
//
// Its one provider is the test runner. Each build of such a context, a
// with of it in a test or one case of a law run under it, gets a fresh
// empty folder under the test's temporary directory (TMPDIR), and the
// runner removes the folder and all it holds when the case ends. Paths
// outside the folder are refused by the providers with their Denied
// failure. A with of such a context stands only in a test.

// Ambient is the test's ambient: a fresh temporary folder per case, which
// only the test runner provides, never the host's Ambient. Its one
// operation is unexported, so no program type implements it and no
// context entry binds it.
// law-exempt: its one operation is unexported, so no law can call it; the confinement it gives is stated by the laws of fstest.Confined, which run over fstest.NewFolder, the Host of fs.NewTestHost in the same folder.
type Ambient {
	folder() string,
}

// Folder is the absolute path of the case's folder, with its symbolic
// links resolved. It exists and is empty when the case starts.
func Folder() string needs Ambient { Ambient.folder() }
